    "created_at": "2023-01-27T15:22:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-27T15:22:24Z",
    "body": "As already written in Discord I would take over this issue. \r\n\r\nAt a first look I noticed the following things:\r\n\r\n- `elapsed` is a u128. However, `std::time::Duration::from_millis()` accepts a `u64`. Is this intentional? If not, I'm happy to adjust it in the same move.\r\n- The `show_milliseconds` option I would probably just remove. That makes the configuration easier. However, the whole thing is only possible if the configuration parser doesn't fail because of it. Do you have an opinion on this?\r\n\r\nIn any case I am looking forward to the first issue on spaceship.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
